workflow-v1.0.json merges GitHub's workflow schema from two repositories, both
distributed under the license below:

- src/Sdk/WorkflowParser/workflow-v1.0.json in https://github.com/actions/runner
  at commit 8cfa1049f86781d141056082d73802d56cd2b433.
- workflow-parser/src/workflow-v1.0.json in
  https://github.com/actions/languageservices at commit
  4043eda158e16579cc5fb1b0b07a4bce2a76f0b5.

The merge keeps every definition and property of either copy. Lists of
contexts, one-of references, and allowed values are joined. Where the copies
give a property different types, the languageservices type is used. Where
they give it the same type and only one requires it, as with "cron", it is not
required, and a string only requires a non-empty value when both copies do.
"repository-dispatch-string" is taken from the runner copy, because the
languageservices constant is wrong.

